!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment.", "type": "text"}]}], "stimuli_ids": [], "template_override": 1, "id": 11, "type": "DWS"}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "id": 0}, {"type": "video", "template_override": 1, "title": "", "_data": [], "contents": [{"type": "video", "value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"time": "100", "image": "", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong notdialogue\">Fingerprinting</span><br /><br />Fingerprinting has been one of the most sophisticated techniques used to screen for, discriminate between and identify guilty persons. However, this technique is not new. It was known thousands of years ago. The first people to use fingerprints for identification were the ancient Assyrians and Chinese, who used fingerprints to sign important documents."}, {"time": "24000", "image": "", "id": 2, "text": "The first modern study of fingerprints was made by Johannes Purkinje, a Czech physiologist. Sir Francis Galton, a British scientist, developed his own system of classifying fingerprints using all ten fingers and ascribing them to their \u201cowners\u201d. Sir Francis' system is the basis of the screening system used today."}, {"time": "45500", "image": "", "id": 3, "text": "The first practical use of fingerprints to identify criminals was in Bengal, India, in the 1890s. This was developed by Sir Edward Richard Henry, a police official. In 1901 he screamed with delight when he created the world's first database of fingerprints."}, {"time": "64000", "image": "", "id": 4, "text": "Today, the use of fingerprints is prescribed around the world. Whenever a person touches any hard, smooth object, a fingerprint made by the oil in the skin is left as if the person has made an inscription in the surface. These prints, which cannot be seen by the naked eye, can be detected using powder or special lights. Police are trained to discover fingerprints on almost any surface. These prints are invaluable in the detection and capture of criminals."}], "video_src": "engenn8le03ob04re2vid01"}}], "id": 2}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Crime and Punishment", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Fingerprinting", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 4, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 3, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Identify and describe rules and obligations though a wider range of language and expressions in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob04re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Consonant Blend /scr/", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Consonant blends are sounds that consist of two or more consonants. They are said together. Sometimes, this can be quite challenging for non-native speakers.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The consonant blend /scr/ consists of three sounds that are said one right after the next. <br /><br />  /s/ + /k/ + /r/ <br /><br />  Say each of these sounds out loud.<br /> Then, say them one right after the next.<br /> Concentrate on what your tongue, teeth and lips are doing.<br /><br />  Practice saying these words:<br /><br /><span class=\"strong\"> screen<br /> scream<br /> discriminate<br /> ascribe<br /> inscription<br /> prescribe<br /></span>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Breaking Sentences into Parts", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you read or speak in English, you often \"chunk\" or break the sentence into parts based on the meaning contained in each part.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Whenever a person touches any hard, smooth object,// a fingerprint made by the oil in the skin// is left as if the person has made// an inscription in the surface. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Sir Francis Galton,// a British scientist,// developed his own system// of classifying fingerprints// using all ten fingers// and ascribing them to their \"owners\". ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "For example, look at the the sentence: <br /><br />  <span class=\"italic\">The first people to use fingerprints for identification were the ancient Assyrians and Chinese, who used fingerprints to sign important documents.</span><br /><br /><br />   This sentence could be chunked or broken into the following parts:<br /><br />  <span class=\"italic\">The first people<br /> to use fingerprints for identification <br /> were the ancient Assyrians and Chinese,<br /> who used fingerprints<br /> to sign important documents.<br /></span>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to screen", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to exclude someone or something after evaluation or investigation", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Fingerprinting has been one of the most sophisticated techniques used to screen for guilty persons.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about crime and punishment.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to discriminate (between)", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to differentiate; to recognize differences", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Fingerprinting has been one of the most sophisticated techniques used to discriminate between guilty persons.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "physiologist ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person who studies the functions of the body", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The first modern study of fingerprints was made by Johannes Purkinje, a Czech physiologist. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to ascribe ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to attribute something to a cause or origin", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sir Francis Galton developed his own system of classifying fingerprints using all ten fingers and ascribing them to their \"owners\".", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "official ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person holding public office or having official duties", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sir Edward Richard Henry was a police official. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob04aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "database", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a collection of information", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He created the world's first database of fingerprints. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob04aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to prescribe", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to recommend", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Today, the use of fingerprints is prescribed around the world.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob04aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "inscription", "type": "name"}, {"content": "words written on a surface", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: A fingerprint made by the oil in the skin is left as if the person has made an inscription in the surface. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob04aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "powder ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "fine dry particles produced by the grinding, crushing, or disintegration of a solid substance", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: These prints, which cannot be seen by the naked eye, can be detected using powder or special lights.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob04aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "With a partner, make a list of all the words you can think of with the <span class=\"italic\">scr</span> sound.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a story using as many of your <span class=\"italic\">scr</span> words as possible.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Practice reading your story aloud to your partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Listen to your partner read the story and help with pronunciation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Exchange stories with another pair of students and practice reading their story aloud.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about rules, crimes and punishment.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I say and use words like <span class=\"italic\">scream</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use proper intonation and stress in long statements.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena"}